course: dictionary
lesson: 756
title: A bazaar is a busy market
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: You can work out what a word means from its context, the words around it. «The Grand Bazaar in Istanbul was started in the 1450s and is one of the oldest and biggest covered markets in the world.» The clues are covered market, oldest and biggest, so a bazaar must be a kind of market.
explain: Bazaar has a second meaning too. At a school or church, a bazaar is a sale that raises money, with cakes, toys and crafts. Ask yourself which meaning fits the sentence. A Christmas bazaar in a school hall is not a street of stalls in Istanbul, so the other words tell you which meaning is meant.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try market in place of bazaar: «The Grand Bazaar in Istanbul is one of the oldest and biggest covered markets in the world.» It still makes sense, so the meaning is right.
fact: A bazaar is a market, especially in the Middle East or South Asia, with many small shops and stalls.
fact: A bazaar can also be a sale held to raise money for a school, church or charity.
fact: A bazaar that is a fundraising sale is also called a fete or a fair.
fact: «The Grand Bazaar» is in Istanbul, and it was started in the 1450s.
fact: A «Christmas bazaar» is a fundraising sale with cakes, toys and crafts.
exercise: «The Grand Bazaar in Istanbul was started in the 1450s.» In this sentence, what kind of place is a bazaar? | A sleepy village with one house | A school hall on a Monday | A mountain path | *A market with many small shops and stalls
exercise: The school has a «Christmas bazaar» on Friday. What is happening? | A long walk to the church | A test in every subject | A football match in the playground | *A fundraising sale with cakes, toys and crafts
exercise: Find and copy the word from «one of the oldest and biggest covered markets» that tells you the market is very old. | biggest | markets | covered | *oldest
test: What is a church bazaar? | *A sale to raise money for the church | A place where people dig for gold | A service where people sing hymns | A tall tower with bells
test: Which sentence uses bazaar to mean a fundraising sale? | The bazaar is a kind of fish | We climbed the bazaar on the hill | *The PTA ran a bazaar to raise money for new library books | The bazaar was a pair of muddy boots
exam: According to the example, which is true of the Grand Bazaar in Istanbul? | *It was started in the 1450s and is a covered market | It was started in the 2000s | It is a small shop in a village | It is a school sale
